Implement user story AMSD-1820: [Mozio] - The Promo code amount is NOT displayed as expected for Return trip tickets in the Mozio email confirmation

## Story Description
[Mozio] - The Promo code amount is NOT displayed as expected for Return trip tickets in the Mozio email confirmation

## Acceptance Criteria
- Given a customer purchases a return trip ticket with a promo code applied, when the Mozio email confirmation is generated, then the promo code discount amount is displayed for BOTH the outbound trip and the return trip, with each leg showing its proportional share of the total promo discount.
- Given a customer purchases a one-way trip with a promo code, when the Mozio email confirmation is generated, then the promo code discount amount continues to display correctly for the single trip (regression check).
- Given a return trip with a promo code where the discount amount is zero, when the Mozio email confirmation is generated, then the email does not show a negative value, NaN, or undefined value for the promo amount on either leg.
- Given a return trip with a promo code, when the email confirmation is rendered, then the sum of the discount amounts shown across both legs equals the total promo code discount value applied at checkout.
- Given a return trip with a promo code discount that results in a fractional-cent amount when split across legs (e.g., $5.01 total discount), when the Mozio email confirmation is generated, then the discount amounts for each leg are displayed with proper currency precision and the sum of both legs still equals the original total discount.
- Given a return trip ticket where the promo discount data is missing or undefined in the report, when the Mozio email confirmation is generated, then the email displays a zero discount for each leg rather than crashing or rendering an error placeholder.
- Given a return trip ticket with a promo code applied, when the discount is split across outbound and return legs, then neither leg displays a discount amount greater than the total promo discount applied at checkout.


## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **src/services/submit-reservations/apply-report-discounts.service.ts** (`getUniqDiscounts`): This function constructs the lineItemId key for each discount from OrderLineItems. The matching logic in applyReportDiscountsService (lines 17-27) parses both discount.lineItemId and dispatch lineItem.id via parseDispatchLineItemKey and compares BOTH id AND isReturn. The dispatch lineItem.id values are built by getDispatchLineItemKey (which appends '#return' for return trips), but getUniqDiscounts likely does NOT use getDispatchLineItemKey when constructing discount.lineItemId — so return-trip discounts get isReturn=false after parsing, causing the match on line 25 (parsedLineItem.isReturn === parsedDiscount.isReturn) to fail for return trips. This is why promo amounts appear for outbound but not return legs.
  - **Minimal fix:** In getUniqDiscounts, when constructing the lineItemId for each LineItemDiscount, use getDispatchLineItemKey(lineItem.id, lineItem.isReturn) instead of just lineItem.id, so that return-trip discounts carry the '#return' suffix and parseDispatchLineItemKey correctly yields isReturn=true. Import getDispatchLineItemKey from '~/services/helpers/order/dispatch-line-item-key' (same import path already used by parseDispatchLineItemKey on line 1).


